---
title: ONI unscramble
tags: tools
heading: "Unscramble"
summary: >-
    Unscrambles a string by swapping each pair of characters, so <code class="tool-example">abcdef</code> becomes <code class="tool-example">badcfe</code>.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>Swapping the pairs again puts them back, so the same tool scrambles and unscrambles. With an odd number of characters, the last one has no pair and is kept as it is. Switch on "Drop an unpaired last character" to leave it out instead, as the original ONI-Tools version does.</p>
    <p>In the browser console: <code class="tool-example">convrtr.{{ filename }}(string, dropUnpaired = false)</code></p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Unscramble", placeholder = "Example: eHll,oW rodl! &srarr; Hello, World!", actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Unscramble" }]) %}
<div class="form-check form-switch">
    <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="{{ filename }}Drop">
    <label class="form-check-label" for="{{ filename }}Drop">Drop an unpaired last character</label>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
